codemap 9
tour feature-edit-text
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note The human writing a tour's note on the Note page of the build-tour wizard, the one place the GUI takes prose: the Tour view has no note editor, and the CLI's tour-note takes the note as one argument. A tour note is the map's prose about a workflow: the 2626 notes in this repo's map average 203 characters and 866 run past 200. The note field was one line: in a run of the wizard on 2026-10-02 a 200-character note showed only its last 60 characters, scrolled sideways; enter left the page (the dump read page=Create), so no paragraph break could be written, and on the Create page enter creates the tour; the middle was reachable only one character at a time; there was no selection and no paste, which TODO.md logged as GUI item 1 ('nothing pastes into a field'). It serves the map as a second channel of prose beside the source, written by the human where tours are built by hand. Two designs were built and run: enter breaks the line and ctrl+enter goes on, in a box that grows from 3 to 12 rows and then scrolls with the caret; and shift+enter breaks the line while enter goes on as on every other wizard page, in a fixed 8-row box. The first was kept: a line break is the key prose needs most, and under the second an enter between paragraphs moves to the Create page, where the next enter creates the tour, as the first run showed; a growing box keeps a short note to three rows. Handing the note to $EDITOR was dropped before building: it leaves the one window, cannot be driven by a script, and needs an editor on PATH. Every text field is one Field type (one concept, one type), so word moves and deletes with alt or ctrl, shift selection, a click that places the caret, a drag that selects, and ctrl+c, ctrl+x and ctrl+v reach the one-line fields too; that is also where TODO's paste item was logged. A script or screenshot run keeps a clipboard of its own, so it never touches the user's.

